WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en-US

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:05.640
The review exercise has three questions.&nbsp;
The first was a general question asking if&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.640 --> 00:00:10.400
the tax variable is required when calling&nbsp;
the calculate_total function. The answer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.400 --> 00:00:17.840
is false because, on line 1, we have a&nbsp;
default value for the tax variable. Thus,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.840 --> 00:00:24.880
if no tax is provided when calling the function,&nbsp;
the default tax rate will be .08. Next, we want to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.880 --> 00:00:31.960
know what the two subtotals will be. For both&nbsp;
subtotals, the amount being taxed is 20,000;&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.960 --> 00:00:39.320
the car amount is 19,000, plus the license&nbsp;
fee is 1000. For the first subtotal,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.320 --> 00:00:49.960
the default tax rate is overridden. 10 percent of&nbsp;
20,000 is 2000, and the sum of those two amounts&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.960 --> 00:00:59.920
is 22,000. For the second subtotal, no tax&nbsp;
rate is specified, so the default rate of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.040 --> 00:01:11.840
8 percent is used. 8 percent of 20,000 is&nbsp;
1600. Add the two, and you have 21,600.

